## 🔍 Root Cause Analysis

### The Five Whys

**1. Why is the orchestration layer dormant?**
- Because no events are being emitted to trigger it.

**2. Why are no events being emitted?**
- Because event emission is manual, not automatic.
- No integration points exist to auto-emit on state changes.

**3. Why is event emission manual?**
- Because the system was designed with orchestration infrastructure first, application integration second.
- The "nervous system" exists, but organs don't connect to it.

**4. Why don't applications connect to the nervous system?**
- Because event emission requires explicit calls ([brain_emit_event()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2401-2405)).
- No hooks/middleware to auto-capture state transitions.

**5. Why are there no auto-capture hooks?**
- **ROOT CAUSE:** Architecture followed "build infrastructure, integrate later" instead of "event-sourced from day one."

